        <type>s32</type>
        <definition>s32 XAsu_SlhdsaSignVerify</definition>
        <argsstring>(XAsu_ClientParams *ClientParamPtr, XAsu_SlhdsaSignVerifyParams *SlhdsaParamPtr)</argsstring>
        <name>XAsu_SlhdsaSignVerify</name>
        <param>
          <type>XAsu_ClientParams *</type>
          <declname>ClientParamPtr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="struct_x_asu___slhdsa_sign_verify_params" kindref="compound">XAsu_SlhdsaSignVerifyParams</ref> *</type>
          <declname>SlhdsaParamPtr</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function sends a command to ASUFW to verify an SLH-DSA signature over the provided message. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ClientParamPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the XAsu_ClientParams structure which holds the client input parameters. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>SlhdsaParamPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the <ref refid="struct_x_asu___slhdsa_sign_verify_params" kindref="compound">XAsu_SlhdsaSignVerifyParams</ref> structure which holds the SLH-DSA signature verification parameters.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS, if IPI request to ASU is sent successfully.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XASU_INVALID_ARGUMENT, if any argument is invalid.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XASU_INVALID_UNIQUE_ID, if the unique ID is invalid.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_FAILURE, if sending an IPI request to ASU fails.</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Success here only means the request was queued; the verdict arrives as XASU_SLHDSA_SIGNATURE_VERIFIED in AdditionalStatus via the callback. CtxLen and CtxAddr must match the values used when the signature was created. </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
